From 9cec671477e6916dbcfaca1b6dc9046e62b65cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 03:08:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: add kernel-protected J773g speaker playback

Add the J773g machine driver on shared MCA, ADMAC and TAS2764 interfaces. Limit playback to mono 48 kHz S24_LE and attenuate and charge sample energy before copying into the DMA ring. Disable mmap and rewinds, and reserve gain controls for the protection policy.

Maintain an integer coil/magnet thermal model across playback sessions, account for held and replayed samples, and monitor DMA progress and amplifier faults. Default the hardware ceiling to -10 dB and mute the amplifier while idle. Expose protection state through sysfs; no userspace protection daemon is required.

Validation: driver objects build and binding schema validation passed. Thermal and progress host regressions pass under ASan/UBSan. Native kernel #109 passed PCM constraints, protected-control checks, underrun recovery, drain and repeated start/drop checks, plus quiet speaker playback. This does not establish a new physical speaker calibration.

Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra)
Assisted-By: Claude Code (Claude Fable 5.1)
Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
